# blog.cole.press lives on as a shortcut to the in-site blog.
# Domain-level from-URL rules are supported by Netlify (2026-11 changelog), but
# this only fires when blog.cole.press is BOUND TO THIS SITE. Right now the
# subdomain is bound to a separate Netlify site that serves a stray empty blog.
# Fix: in the Netlify dashboard, detach blog.cole.press from that site and add
# it as a domain alias of the cole.press site; this rule then does the rest.
https://blog.cole.press/*  https://cole.press/blog/:splat  301

# Legacy .html URLs → clean URLs (keep the site's links .html-proof)
/index.html                  /  301
/about.html                  /about  301
/research.html               /research  301
/projects.html               /projects  301
/cv/index.html               /cv/  301
/colophon.html               /colophon  301
/portfolio/index.html        /portfolio/  301
/portfolio/photos.html       /portfolio/photos  301
/portfolio/writing.html      /portfolio/writing  301
/blog/index.html             /blog/  301
